direct-defer-any
owner: opus-5 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: operator's ask: make a NON-tail mutual call work without
  !.tailcall too. The only complete rule is "defer every program-typed
  call in a block", and its cost lands on all direct-style code, not
  just recursive: DirectBenchmark.okayDirect marks 10 000 calls per
  iteration. So this lane MEASURES first — implement, run okayDirect /
  okayDirectRec against master with -prof gc, and let the number decide
  between shipping it, keeping !.tailcall for the non-tail case, or a
  cheaper shape (a single-node deferring Bind).
files: src/main/scala/Direct.scala, src/test/scala/TestDirectDeep.scala,
  docs, specs/direct-macro.md, CHANGELOG.md
